 Review comment:
   Yes. The previous method was used on both the client and server sides to get access to the created server. A server would be created both if a server registered a port, and if a client requested a port. This required thread safety for the reason you mention, so you don't end up with the client and server side seeing different LocalServer instances.

   This method is only called by the server side, and the client accesses the generated server via `_registry.get`. Since we don't have multiple servers binding to the same node/port combination, we don't need to worry about overlapping calls to this method. Clients won't create servers anymore, but instead just buffer messages until the server gets bound by the server side thread.

