 Review comment:
   I cleaner solution, I think, is to change RedundancyLogger to PersistentBucketRecoverer. One of the things this class would do, it what it does now; log information on how persistent bucket recovery is doing. But that other thing it would do is own the allBucketsRecoveredFromDisk latch. The redundancyProvider would no longer have this latch. It already has an instance variable referring to the RedundancyLogger (you would need to change this to be volatile as the latch currently is). The methods that want to wait for recovery to complete will now just call a method on PersistentBucketRecoverer. Basically any work with this latch should be implemented on the PersistentBucketRecoverer. The provider will just check to see if its PersistentBucketRecoverer is not null and if it has one delegate to it.

