 Review comment:
   I summarized suggestions from Kenn and me. 

   It is better to split this method into two parts:
   1. skip row if needed
   2. do standard processing.
   This will make reading code much easier.

   toSkipRows initialization might need some update.
   ```suggestion
         Integer toSkipRows = firstNonNull(skippedRowsState.read(), startIndex);
         if (toSkipRows > 0) {
             skippedRowsState.write(toSkipRows - 1);
             return;
         }

         int current = (counterState.read() != null ? counterState.read() : 0);
         if (current < limitCount) {
           counterState.write(current + 1);
           context.output(context.element().getValue());
         }
   ```

